;
; How Sieve indexes one held suggestion in MYRA (sieve_rules.h SR5): its
; own id (10 digits), the app it is for (a slot, 3 digits), its source (0
; answer, 1 draft, 2 envelope), its state (1 pending, 2 accepted,
; 3 rejected, 4 applied: zxm.h M3 and sieve_model.h SM2), the second its
; hold lapses (12 digits, to the year 9999) and the version of the target
; it was made against (18 digits). Sieve asks whether the numbers fit
; before it keeps them.
^ZXSIEVE(id:i10) = app:i3! ^ source:i1! ^ state:i1! ^ expires:i12! ^ version:i18!
